          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>\"Tristes Tropiques\" and Reflections</strong><br>\nLévi-Strauss's \"Tristes Tropiques,\" published in 1955, blends travel writing with anthropological study and philosophical reflection. It offers a critical look at Western civilization from the perspective gained through his fieldwork.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Mythology and \"The Raw and the Cooked\"</strong><br>\nHis four-volume mythological study beginning with \"The Raw and the Cooked\" further explored the structural analysis of myths, emphasizing the binaries and symmetries that he believed form the basis of human thought.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on Anthropology and Other Fields</strong><br>\nLévi-Strauss's work impacted not only anthropology but also linguistics, philosophy, and literary studies. His idea of the \"bricoleur\" and the \"savage mind\" challenged conventional views of the evolution of human cognition and cultural expression.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
