            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Challenges to His Theories</strong><br>\nWhile Lévi-Strauss's theories were influential, they were also controversial, with debates about their applicability to diverse cultures and their sometimes deterministic implications.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Honors</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Lévi-Strauss continued to write and lecture, becoming a member of the French Academy and receiving numerous honors for his work. He remained active in the academic field well into his 90s.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nLévi-Strauss died on October 30, 2009, at the age of 100. His work remains a cornerstone of anthropological theory, and his method of structural analysis is still debated and studied in anthropology and other disciplines today.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3d655444-fd55-42f7-aba2-16a16db7dc58"
